# Local demo cases

Catalogue of local Manage Cases examples for design review. Each entry links to a seeded CCD
case and explains what state or journey the case demonstrates.

Case references are created by `./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh` and change every time you clear
and re-seed. They are **not** committed — regenerate them on your machine after
`./gradlew bootWithCCD` is running.

Catalogue PCNs use the catalogue authority's TEC id. The default is Westminster, so **Penalty
charge number** starts with `WE` and the suffix is `0`. What each character means, and how the
check digit is calculated: [Penalty charge numbers](/penalty-charge-numbers.html).

Approach, scenario list, and how to customise the catalogue:
[Local demo catalogue seed](http://localhost:4568/demo-catalogue-seed.html)
(tech docs), including
[Customising the catalogue](http://localhost:4568/demo-catalogue-seed.html#customising-the-catalogue).

## Prerequisites

1. Stack up: `./gradlew bootWithCCD`
2. Manage Cases via the nav proxy: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
   (sign in as `tec-demo@test.com` / `password`)
3. Seed:

```bash
./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh
```

Then refresh this page. Middleman will pick up the generated links partial.

